; The level of a glide. A frame that glides its own filter go towards halfway to a neighbour's gn speaks more
; quietly than go, which its gain was made for. Per frame three cards in (gn, go, w, as glideb reads them); two
; out for the level's last step, after the number of the record of the glide table it asks the host for: mode 0
; and 0 without a glide (w 10, record 0 asked for and passed over), else mode 4 and the factor c (in percent) that
; puts the power back. c is card 3 gn + 0, 1 or 2 (for w 3, 5 or 9) of record go: it reads all 291 of the record's
; cards, keeping that one.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            frm     INP   gn       03-18: a frame; no glide, mode 0
  04                    INP   go
  05                    INP   w
  06                    CLA   z
  07                    STO   c
  08                    STO   m
  09                    CLA   w
  10                    SUB   ten
  11                    TAC   gl
  12                    CLA   m1
  13                    STO   p
  14                    CLA   z
  15                    STO   go
  16                    JMP   ask
  17            gl      CLA   four
  18                    STO   m
  19                    CLA   gn       19-34: p = 3 gn, + 1 for w 5, + 2 for w 9
  20                    ADD   gn
  21                    ADD   gn
  22                    STO   p
  23                    CLA   w
  24                    SUB   five
  25                    TAC   ask
  26                    CLA   p
  27                    ADD   00
  28                    STO   p
  29                    CLA   w
  30                    SUB   nine
  31                    TAC   ask
  32                    CLA   p
  33                    ADD   00
  34                    STO   p
  35            ask     OUT   go       35-52: record go, card p kept
  36                    CLA   n290
  37                    STO   i
  38            gc      INP   x
  39                    CLA   p
  40                    SUB   00
  41                    STO   p
  42                    TAC   chk
  43                    JMP   nx
  44            chk     ADD   00       (p was 0: this card)
  45                    TAC   nx
  46                    CLA   x
  47                    STO   c
  48            nx      CLA   i
  49                    SUB   00
  50                    STO   i
  51                    TAC   out
  52                    JMP   gc
  53            out     OUT   m        53-70: the mode and c
  54                    OUT   c
  55                    JMP   frm
  56            gn      DATA  0
  57            go      DATA  0
  58            w       DATA  0
  59            p       DATA  0
  60            i       DATA  0
  61            x       DATA  0
  62            c       DATA  0
  63            z       DATA  0
  64            ten     DATA  10
  65            five    DATA  5
  66            nine    DATA  9
  67            four    DATA  4
  68            n290    DATA  290
  69            m       DATA  0
  70            m1      DATA  -1
